    <sys:String x:Key="Servers.BootstrapHint">Bootstrap IPs prevent recursive interception while an encrypted endpoint connects.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Failover.DefaultChain">Default chain ID</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Failover.Hint">Resolvers are tried from left to right. Separate server IDs with commas; failed resolvers enter a temporary cooldown.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Rules.Hint">Rules are evaluated from top to bottom.</sys:String>

    <sys:String x:Key="Protection.Title">Windows enforcement</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Protection.Description">The signed WinDivert kernel driver captures outbound UDP DNS before a VPN or another local resolver can take it. Explicit TCP port 53 is blocked fail-closed while encrypted upstreams use ports 443 or 853.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Protection.EnableEnforcement">Enable DNS enforcement</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Protection.BlockTcp">Block explicit TCP DNS leaks in the kernel network stack</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Protection.Interval">Enforcement check interval (seconds)</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Protection.Limit">BetterDNS does not inspect HTTPS: application-owned DoH on port 443 cannot be distinguished from normal web traffic without weakening TLS. DNS packet interception is kernel-level; encrypted resolver and policy logic remains isolated in the LocalSystem service.</sys:String>

